tle of attrition where one  player can turn the tide changing a  three versus one match into an even bout  or turning the tables completely to gain  the upper hand it's worth noting that  Gears of War 4 does suffer from some  technical issues in both its multiplayer  and story modes certain objectives  didn't trigger during my campaign  forcing me to restart the last  checkpoint and replay sometimes boring  chapters the game also froze several  times in the menus as it tried to load a  match or even just the next menu page  these problems don't ruin the overall  experience but they're irritating enough  to cast a pallor over some of the games  sections  and that serves as a microcosm for the  entirety of Gears of War for this is a  shooter teetering on the edge of  something greater  but despite the improvements it makes to  the storied franchise its missteps hold  it back there is inspiration here and  creativity in the way Gears of War for  rethinks its multiplayer modes but the  lackluster campaign and technical issues  are blights on an otherwise exhilarating  shooter the result is a hole that  doesn't reflect the quality of its often  stellar parts not a goddamn word  [Applause]  you
 

